    "intro_html":  "Tetrazzini sounds Italian, but it was invented in San Francisco and named after an opera singer, which makes it about as American as a casserole gets. Spaghetti and turkey bound in a mushroom cream sauce, covered in mozzarella and parmesan, baked until the top blisters. Each serving carries \u003cstrong\u003e42 grams of protein\u003c/strong\u003e and 621 calories for about \u003cstrong\u003e$4.86\u003c/strong\u003e (at everyday cost). That is a restaurant pasta plate for less than the tip.",
